  "definition": "DRS refers to the Disability Rating Scale, a standardized measure used to track overall functional change during recovery after moderate to severe traumatic brain injury. It looks at areas such as alertness and responsiveness, cognitive ability for self-care, dependence on others, and psychosocial adaptation.",
